{{=<% %>=}}## Runtime flags for <%name%>.

## NO ERLANG DISTRIBUTION LISTENER. The service talks to the mesh, never to
## another Erlang node, and answers /health on a Unix socket. relx's start
## script demands a node name, so the node has a short one, but it starts no
## epmd and never listens for a node connection, and it has no cookie: no
## remote shell or dist-eval can reach the process that holds this service's
## keys (mcl-om#24). A service that genuinely needs distribution adds `-name',
## a cookie from the environment and `-kernel inet_dist_use_interface
## {127,0,0,1}' -- and says why in its README.
-sname <%name%>
-start_epmd false
-dist_listen false

+K true

## Async thread pool. Raise it only if this service does real file or port I/O;
## for CPU-bound work the schedulers are the resource that matters and this flag
## is not on that path.
+A 8
